<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huanggang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huanggang is a city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubei">Hubei</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the north bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a>. Its area was the site of Zhu, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-rui">Wu Rui</a>'s Kingdom of Hengshan after 206 BCE. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> poet Su Shi spent his exile there at Huangzhou, where he wrote his famous 'Red Cliff' pieces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huanggang.jpg" alt="Huanggang" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 刘心宇 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E9%BB%84%E5%86%88%E5%A4%A9%E9%99%85%E7%BA%BF.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
